   "statement": "The property-tax relief and the exchange compete for the same years. Claiming the intergenerational exclusion means making the home the principal residence; qualifying a dwelling unit for an exchange means renting it at a fair rental and keeping personal use to the greater of 14 days or 10% of the rental days in each of two 12-month periods. A household cannot do both with the same two years, and a home used solely as a personal residence does not qualify at all.",
